"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
246,"Sufyan narrated to us, Ayoub bin Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, who is the son of Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari. H Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Musa, on the authority of Al Maqbari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rafi’, On the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: I said, O Messenger of God, I am a woman who has tightened the braids of my head, so take it off to wash it. Impurity? He said: “It is enough for you to throw three handfuls of water on your head, then pour water over yourself and be cleansed,” or he said: “Then you She has been purified.” This is the hadith of Al-Makhzoumi, and Abdul-Jabbar said: “Then you have been purified,” and he did not say: “Then you will be purified.”"
247,"We are Imran bin Musa Al-Qazzaz, we are Abdul-Warith, meaning Ibn Saeed Al-Anbari. H Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Abu Ammar said: Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, and he said Al-Dawraqi: Ibn Ulayya, who is Ismail bin Ibrahim, all of us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, he said: He reported Aisha said that Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas commanded his wives to cut off their heads when they had done ablution from ritual impurity, so she said, “Oh I wonder, this Ibn Amr has cost them a lot of trouble. Should he not order them to shave their heads when it was me and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. We wash from one vessel, all of us in it, but no more than three handfuls,” or he said: “three handfuls.” This is the hadith of Abd al-Warith, and it is not in the hadith of Ibn Ulayya: We all start with it, and he said in it: “I will not do more than pour on my head three ""emptions"""
